codex
The boundary check found two supplied-model limitations, not a substituted proof: MPY’s `<=` treats NaN as ordered (so its result differs from CPython), and its concrete Int→Float hook aborts on an enormous integer where CPython raises `OverflowError`. Both originate in the fixed read-only semantics; the submitted Python itself follows CPython. I’ll record these as explicit trust-ledger concerns with concrete witnesses.
